Z||000000||rogergarrison||07-24-2001||03:31 PM||||I have 3800 GM . Its been working perfectly. this morning I started it and gauge shows discharge. Battery w/load checks with meter/tester at 12.5 volts so thats ok. The alternator tester shows only putting out 12 volts, should be 13.5-16 volts. I replaced with new one. still same reading, all wiring looks to be fine, batt connections fine,recent new EMC. Im now also getting 'check anti lock' but I think thats just because of low charging, theyve been disconnected for a year. anyone have any more ideas?||||reg||1
Z||000001||PBJ||07-24-2001||03:41 PM||||you will need to get a schematic on the feed/signal wire for alt. see if alt has signal voltage?||||reg||1
Z||000002||starfighter007@msn.com||07-24-2001||04:01 PM||||I would not trust your new alternator.It also could have bad voltage regulator in it.This would not be the first time a replacement alternator or starter was bad defective right from the parts house.I would take it back to where you bought it from.||||reg||1
Z||000003||rogergarrison||07-24-2001||04:41 PM||||thats true star, Ive had that happen too. Gonna let the garage next door look at it and see if they get any codes. Someone says newer engines also get a signal from ecm to tell the alt to charge. so maybe sitting in the hot sun fried something in the ecm thats about 2 months old.||||reg||1
